This is Erdős Problem 952, the Gaussian moat problem — a genuine open problem in number theory. It asks whether there exists an infinite sequence of distinct Gaussian primes with uniformly bounded gaps. This remains unsolved; the best known results only establish finite connected clusters of Gaussian primes of bounded step size, and no infinite path with bounded jumps is known to exist.

